<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="41ac0f87-cf3d-5a2a-86a8-f70b1f6aab1a" activityNameId="ad8496b8-253a-5fc4-a6f5-31a2df058cd0" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Single cell, lithium-ion battery, lithium manganese oxide/graphite, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Single cell, lithium-ion battery, lithium manganese oxide/graphite, at plant
The dataset can be used as a cathode for a lithium-ion battery. Data are based on patents. For infrastructure, the ecoinvent dataset "chemical plant, organics" is accounted. Transportation efforts are based on ecoinvent standard estimates.;
UUID: a748abc6-4058-372d-bf9d-6bfd24d954ea
This dataset incudes the production of a single cell for a lithium ion battery. Cathode, anode and a seperator are calendared. An aluminium electrode tab is added. The singel cells are filled with electrolyte (LiPF6 in ethylencarbonate) in an inert atmosphere and packed up in a polyethylene envelope.  For infrastructure, the ecoinvent dataset "chemical plant, organics" is accounted. Transportation efforts are based on ecoinvent standard estimates.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: This dataset includes a method of producing a lithium ion single cell. Lithium ion move from the cathode (LiMn2O4) into the electrolyte (LiPF6 in ethylenecarbonate) through the micropores of the sepeartor into the anode (lithium ion intercalation). During the charging phase. During the discharge of the battery the Li+-ions move back into the cathode. 
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: measurements, patent, ecoinvent 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: Uncertainty is assessed using the pedigree matrix.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a748abc6-4058-372d-bf9d-6bfd24d954ea.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="3142d8e2-0d30-557e-b090-9faae2b72357" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
